{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And YHWH looked upon the camp of Egypt in a pillar of fire and cloud.</b> The two pillars that were moving in the middle of the space between the camp of Egypt and the camp of Israel — He brought them near to the side of the camp of Egypt." "<b>And He threw [them] into panic.</b> With kinds of diseases, as in the case of the Philistines: וַתְּהִי יַד ה' בָּעִיר מְהוּמָה גְּדוֹלָה מְאֹד, וַיַּךְ אֶת אַנְשֵׁי הָעִיר מִקָּטֹן וְעַד גָּדוֹל, וַיִּשָּׂתְרוּ לָהֶם עֳפָלִים (1 Samuel 5:9). And those kinds of diseases are the מַדְוֵי מִצְרַיִם הָרָעִים (Deuteronomy 7:15), and this is הַיָּד הַגְּדוֹלָה אֲשֶׁר עָשָׂה ה' בְּמִצְרַיִם (Exodus 14:31) which Israel saw and feared, as it says: אֲשֶׁר יָגֹרְתָּ מִפָּנֶיהָם (Deuteronomy 28:60). Indeed, the specific plagues that the Torah mentioned contained no disease other than boils — and behold, the Torah mentioned שְׁחִין מִצְרַיִם (Deuteronomy 28:27) and also mentioned מַדְוֵי מִצְרַיִם."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:25:36.281138827Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}